  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Field trials for improved forage crops with Kenyan dairy cooperatives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to develop the dairy sector in Kenya regarding access to proper feed (grass) for the livestock. In Kenya, there is a lack of proper seeds for forage, which is an opportunity for Dutch parties to provide the necessary knowledge and services to build a good foundation for better seeds for forage in Kenya. In this project, field trials are organised for improved forage crops with the Baringo Agricultural Marketing Service Cooperative Society in Baringo County and Tarakwo Cooperative in Uasin County. Cooperatives and Kenyan institutes such as KEPHIS will be involved in developing new forage species to scale and adapt the formal testing procedures and criteria to the present international standards.</narrative>
  </description>
